From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: gregordinary <33880035+gregordinary@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 27 Aug 2026 22:01:36 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] media: rkvdec: do not dereference a NULL context in the
 interrupt handler

rkvdec_irq_handler() resolves the current job's context with
v4l2_m2m_get_curr_priv() and hands it to the variant handler without
checking it. That function returns NULL when no job is current, and every
variant handler opens with

	struct rkvdec_dev *rkvdec = ctx->dev;

so an interrupt taken with nothing in flight faults in the handler.

Return IRQ_NONE instead. With no job current there is nothing to complete,
which is what IRQ_NONE says, and it is the right answer whether the
interrupt is spurious, shared, or raised by a device that has been left
asserting after a job was already finished.

Signed-off-by: gregordinary <33880035+gregordinary@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 drivers/media/platform/rockchip/rkvdec/rkvdec.c | 8 ++++++++
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/media/platform/rockchip/rkvdec/rkvdec.c b/drivers/media/platform/rockchip/rkvdec/rkvdec.c
index 14501fb7d..5a4faf958 100644
--- a/drivers/media/platform/rockchip/rkvdec/rkvdec.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/rockchip/rkvdec/rkvdec.c
@@ -1553,6 +1553,14 @@ static irqreturn_t rkvdec_irq_handler(int irq, void *priv)
 	struct rkvdec_ctx *ctx = v4l2_m2m_get_curr_priv(rkvdec->m2m_dev);
 	const struct rkvdec_variant *variant = rkvdec->variant;
 
+	/*
+	 * Every variant handler reaches the device through the context, so an
+	 * interrupt taken with no job current has nothing to complete and
+	 * nothing to dereference.
+	 */
+	if (!ctx)
+		return IRQ_NONE;
+
 	return variant->ops->irq_handler(ctx);
 }
 
